When I want something crunchy instead of soft bread, I reach for this Swedish crispbread. In Sweden this kind of bread is called knäckebröd, or hårt bröd, which just means "hard bread." The ingredients are about as simple as it gets: whole grain rye flour and salt. No sugar, no wheat flour, nothing else.

I mostly eat it with [hummus](/recipes/hummus) or natural peanut butter with no added sugar. The protein and fat make it a really satisfying snack that doesn't spike my blood sugar the way regular crackers can.

Nutrition is per serving of 2 slices. It keeps for months in the pantry, and you can find it in the cracker aisle at most grocery stores.
